      "text": "To convert the given spherical coordinates \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5\\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)\\) to rectangular coordinates \\((x, y, z)\\), we use the following conversion formulas:\n\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi\n\\]\n\nGiven the spherical coordinates:\n\\[\n\\rho = 3, \\quad \\theta = \\frac{5\\pi}{12}, \\quad \\phi = 0\n\\]\n\nFirst, we evaluate each component separately.\n\n1. **Calculate \\(x\\):**\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta\n\\]\nSince \\(\\phi = 0\\), \\(\\sin \\phi = \\sin 0 = 0\\):\n\\[\nx = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\cos \\left( \\frac{5\\pi}{12} \\right) = 0\n\\]\n\n2. **Calculate \\(y\\):**\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta\n\\]\nSince \\(\\phi = 0\\), \\(\\sin \\phi = \\sin 0 = 0\\):\n\\[\ny = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\sin \\left( \\frac{5\\pi}{12} \\right) = 0\n\\]\n\n3. **Calculate \\(z\\):**\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi\n\\]\nSince \\(\\phi = 0\\), \\(\\cos \\phi = \\cos 0 = 1\\):\n\\[\nz = 3 \\cdot 1 = 3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the rectangular coordinates are:\n\\[\n(x, y, z) = (0, 0, 3)\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}\n\\]",
