      "text": "Given the spherical coordinates \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5\\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)\\), we need to convert these to rectangular coordinates \\((x, y, z)\\).\n\nThe formulas for the conversion from spherical coordinates to rectangular coordinates are:\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi\n\\]\n\nGiven \\(\\rho = 3\\), \\(\\theta = \\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\), and \\(\\phi = 0\\), we can substitute these values into the formulas.\n\nFirst, calculate \\(\\sin \\phi\\), \\(\\cos \\phi\\), \\(\\sin \\theta\\), and \\(\\cos \\theta\\):\n\\[\n\\sin \\phi = \\sin 0 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos \\phi = \\cos 0 = 1\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin \\theta = \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\cos \\frac{5\\pi}{12}\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(y\\) using the formula \\(y = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta\\):\n\\[\ny = 3 \\sin 0 \\sin \\theta = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} = 0\n\\]\n\nNow, calculate \\(x\\) using the formula \\(x = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta\\):\n\\[\nx = 3 \\sin 0 \\cos \\theta = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\cos \\frac{5\\pi}{12} = 0\n\\]\n\nFinally, calculate \\(z\\) using the formula \\(z = \\rho \\cos \\phi\\):\n\\[\nz = 3 \\cos 0 = 3 \\cdot 1 = 3\n\\]\n\nPutting it all together, the rectangular coordinates are:\n\\[\n(x, y, z) = (0, 0, 3)\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}\n\\]",
