      "text": "$\\rho = \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2} = 3$ so $x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 9$.\n$0 = \\arccos \\left( \\frac{z}{\\rho} \\right) \\Rightarrow \\cos (0) = \\frac{z}{3} \\Rightarrow z = 0$.\n$\\frac{5\\pi}{12} = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{y}{x} \\right) \\Rightarrow \\tan \\left( \\frac{5\\pi}{12} \\right) = \\frac{y}{x} \\Rightarrow y = \\frac{x}{2}$.\n$x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 9 \\Rightarrow x^2 + \\left( \\frac{x}{2} \\right)^2 = 9 \\Rightarrow \\frac{5}{4}x^2 = 9 \\Rightarrow x^2 = \\frac{36}{5} \\Rightarrow x = \\pm \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}}$.\nSince $x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 9$ and $z = 0$, $y = \\frac{x}{2}$ implies $y = \\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}$.\nTherefore, the rectangular coordinates are $\\boxed{\\left( \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}}, \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}, 0 \\right)}$ or $\\boxed{\\left( -\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}}, -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}, 0 \\right)}$. The final answer is: \\boxed{\\left( \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}}, \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}, 0 \\right)} \\text{ or } \\boxed{\\left( -\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}}, -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}, 0 \\right)}",
